 "assumptions":
 [{"text":
   "\"Anyone on the bridge must have the torch\": a crossing moves the torch with the people; the torch is at a side, like the people.",
   "stmts": [2, 6],
   "kind": "intent",
   "id": "A-BT1"},
  {"text":
   "Elapsed minutes are a number on a clock object, starting at 0; each crossing adds its time with the new update effect.",
   "stmts": [4, 5, 7],
   "kind": "intent",
   "id": "A-BT2"},
  {"text":
   "\"at the speed of the slower one\": cross-two takes a faster person a and a slower person b (b.minutes > a.minutes) and adds b's minutes, so no maximum is needed and each pair is proposed once. All four times differ; equal times would need >= and would propose a pair twice.",
   "stmts": [5],
   "kind": "intent",
   "id": "A-BT3"},
  {"text":
   "\"the other side\": a static other relation between the two sides, both ways.",
   "stmts": [1, 6],
   "kind": "intent",
   "id": "A-BT4"},
  {"text":
   "\"within 17 minutes\" asks for a fast crossing, so a crossing's minutes are also its step cost, and the task searches by cost (flags iterative-step cost, which brings cost-metric unit): iterative deepening on a cost cap, the library's IDA*. The clock still decides the losing state.",
   "stmts": [4, 7],
   "kind": "intent",
   "id": "A-BT6"},
  {"text":
   "Search control, not from the English (as decided by JL on 16 Nov 2026 for the river crossings): a look-ahead state that returns to a situation already on its path fails. A situation is where each person and the torch are; the clock is not part of it, so going back and forth is cut off even though it changes the time.",
   "stmts": [],
   "kind": "intent",
   "id": "A-BT7"},
  {"text":
   "\"within 17 minutes\": more than 17 elapsed minutes is a losing state; the goal itself tests only where the people are.",
   "stmts": [7],
   "kind": "intent",
   "id": "A-BT5"}]}
